{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1096650-the-book-of-modern-dreams-project","id":1096650,"title":"The Book of Modern Dreams Project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T01:16:48-07:00","id":1096650,"title":"The Book of Modern Dreams Project","content":"Several people have expressed interest in Jane_Dargason\u2019s and my \u2018Book of Modern Dreams\u2019 project from the old Shadownessence forum, so we thought we would make a public thread for anyone that wants to give us feedback and input! We\u2019ll use this to give updates on the project, and hopefully glean enough glamour from it to keep us going to completion!<br /> <br /> So without further ado, here is an outline of what we have brainstormed so far for the book:<br /> <br /> Urban Legends \u2013 How the Modern Dream has affected the changelings and the Dreaming, and details on city freeholds and dreams.<br /> <br /> To Infinity and Beyond \u2013 The impact of the Space-age Dream, and introducing the alien kith, the Grey, along with their thallain counterpart.<br /> <br /> A Dreamer\u2019s High \u2013 Exploring the history and relationship between the Dreaming and mind-altering substances, how the \u2018War on Drugs\u2019 has affected the Dreaming, and introducing the bizarre Gallain called Narcotics.<br /> <br /> Post-Humanism \u2013 Delving deeper into the Modern Inanime, focusing on three specific phyla: the Mannikin ask what it is to be \u2018human\u2019, the Flickers, which are a much older phyla than many realize, and the A.I. elementals of Machina. These latter Inanima freak out even the Mannikin, and the \u2018Ghosts-in-the-Shell\u2019 have many worrying implications for the Inanime as a whole.<br /> <br /> Modern Nightmares \u2013 Exploring the thallain and darker-things of the Modern Dream. Including the Slender, Rippers, Darkly (mirror entities), and others.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that about covers the big ideas. Each section already has had a ton of research, and even some initial brainstorming, but all that is now being reviewed in light of C20 (especially the Inanime). We would love to hear peoples thoughts and ideas, and will keep posting here as things progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T07:46:18-07:00","id":1096713,"title":"","content":"That's great! I'll post any ideas and sugestions, when I'll have any... Or now I guess.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling, that aliens (especially, those based on a Lovecraft, H.R. Giger) might b\u0443 more interesting as Adhene, who have a connection with Autumn World (Like Aonides, for example), rather than another kind of magical people. Though, the isolated village of kinains, affected by &quot;Deep Ones&quot; might be cool. =)<br /> <br /> <b>A Dreamer's High</b> sounds a lot like a name of Changeling high school in Idealized Oregon, which is an interesting concept in itself for a write-up. Wellm think about it.<br /> <br /> Also, really. What's with idealized Oregon (Life is Strange) and Portland (Portlandia)? Judging by myths about the place it looks, like new kithain haven, on par with San-Francisco. Just a footnote.<br /> <br /> Realms on the Edge - detailing using of Realms on modern stuff. Maybe suggesting which dots can be used on what or changing/dividing Props into tangible (clothes, weapons, robots, hardware) and intangible (waves, light, data, software) aspects.<br /> <br /> Post-Humanism - Yay!<br /> <br /> Modern media and media icons. The brief history of the media from he oral traditions to the Internet. Television, books, graphic novels, webcomics, anime. Like, do you remember, when the radio play of Wells' &quot;War of the Worlds&quot; scared the hell out of everyone? Imagine caped superheroes traversing the sky of Near Dreaming. Teenage music idols, who gather an insane following. Social media, sheer collective Glamour of which is only overshadowed by its collective Banality. You can be ruined in the instant by these new mobs... or exalted. Connectedness and anxiety of modern age. Postmodernist art of myth-making, creative cynicism.<br /> <br /> It's more of thought-stream, Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-25-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:02:40-07:00","id":1096717,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered about the Power of Fandom and its impact on the Dreaming. Considering the amount of roleplay, fanfic, and fan worship that some fandoms inspire (Harry Potter, Supernatural, to name a few) I wonder if actual chimera that take the shape of these fictional characters could form, Incidental or Dreamed. I can very much imagine Hogwarts in the Near Dreaming. It would certainly make for an interesting adventure as a fanboy gets sucked into an adventure in his fandom and local changelings need to go rescue him.<br /> <br /> <b>ETA: </b>Just think about all the chimera that could pop up around a gaming/anime/comic convention amidst all the cosplayers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:47:07-07:00","id":1096778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1096650-the-book-of-modern-dreams-project?p=1096713#post1096713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's great! I'll post any ideas and sugestions, when I'll have any... Or now I guess.<br /> <br /> Like, do you remember, when the radio play of Wells' &quot;War of the Worlds&quot; scared the hell out of everyone?<br /> It's more of thought-stream, Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you brought that one up actually! That was going to be the 'Resurgence' for the Grey as a kith.<br /> <br /> The idea is, that because of the mists, and their Dream being of the unknown to begin with, even the Grey themselves aren't sure how old they are. Some do HAVE memories of interacting with ancient human civilizations (I may have had a sick day and been watching Ancient Aliens when I was developing the Grey :P ) but it isn't clear if they are actual memories, or imagined ones made retrospectively by human belief. This idea was actually a big part of a lot of the Modern Dreams.<br /> <br /> I have a lang flight coming up this weekend, so I'll try to type some stuff up/ edit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:17:32-07:00","id":1097128,"title":"","content":"Another potential Modern kith I am currently working the kinks out of does tie into the Power of Fandom as well as Hope, Heroism, and dreams; Mahou, the Magical Girls and Boys. I'm tempted to make a Thallain counterpart for them as well but I am unsure how I would go about it.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of Grey Mythos is also how they often seem to be working with other Alien Races and what might those Other Aliens possibly be for our Modern Dreams Setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:46:27-07:00","id":1097177,"title":"","content":"Does Mahou Birthrights include Transformation Sequence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well... <br /> <br /> You could call it &quot;Cursed Child&quot; or something. The Force of Hatred, Despair and Torment, that rots and twists everything it touches. Good example might include Rowling's Obscurials. The idea is that they are a nightnare of own nature being rejected until pathology, either by subject or the environment.<br /> <br /> Though, might be too close to the concept of Dauntain...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:55:18-07:00","id":1097182,"title":"","content":"Could you consider adding sidebars with suggestions for c2e for those, who might not use particular c20 retcons?<br /> <br /> You said, you made it for 2nd edition. Maybe you don't need to throw out everything you made for it. Just an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T16:38:20-07:00","id":1097351,"title":"","content":"I don't think we were going to chop much, buthat a little editing would be in order. For example, I was working on a Thallain Art called Insidiousness, whose dot 5 cantrip was Possession. Problem is, that's Oneromancy's dot 5 now, so I'll need to re-think it. <br /> <br /> The only ones I'm really unsure about are the Inanime. I really dislike the 'unleashing only' thing as it currently stands, but hats why I thought I'd leave the Slivers be for the time being. Plenty of other stuff to work on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T16:40:12-07:00","id":1097352,"title":"","content":"Although, I should add, sidebars are maybe one of my favorite things to work on. It's like the writing equivalent of turning to the camera to talk to the audience. I feel like Deadpoold","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T23:09:31-07:00","id":1097434,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure, this is a right place to comment on that, but I plan to ignore the fifth dot of Oneiromancy as it is.<br /> <br /> Possession is a cool power, no problem, overall but sometimes I think, that Cantrips, as is, should be remade into something like Exalted Charm Trees. They're too bloody variable for a theme, both in application and intention...<br /> <br /> I like side notes in Dresden Files RPG and Accelerated, made by in-universe characters. Writer and character arguing would be totally a like Deadpool. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-27-2017, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T17:32:22-07:00","id":1098623,"title":"","content":"Huh...the effects of the modern Dreaming from the Autumn world are interesting but the creation of new Kiths and Gallain sends off warning signs: how did the Greys learn the changeling way? What does it mean if new kinds of fae are born into the world on the cusp of the Long Winter?<br /> Not dealbreakers, but something to remember and an interesting sidebar at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:48:16-07:00","id":1101619,"title":"","content":"<b>To Infinity and Beyond</b> really catches my attention, and stimulates my imagination. Many ancient cultures thought True Fae like beings and even humans dwelt on the Moon and among the Stars. The stories attached to constellations alone would generate a great deal of glamour, not to mention all of the people who really <i>believe </i>in horoscopes. Old gods, stellar fae, living stars and life on distant worlds, lots to choose from to be sure. <br /> <br /> The starry sky of the Dreaming (even the Near Dreaming), Moon and Star trods, and the strange chimera of the heavens give a great many opportunities for enterprising fae to tap into these dreams. And with the many stories of UFO's, abductions, extraterrestrials (who look like Sidhe, Dragons and Goblins), science-fiction, and every report of Exoplanets, this is fertile ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T14:09:49-07:00","id":1103918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1096650-the-book-of-modern-dreams-project?p=1098623#post1098623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh...the effects of the modern Dreaming from the Autumn world are interesting but the creation of new Kiths and Gallain sends off warning signs: how did the Greys learn the changeling way? What does it mean if new kinds of fae are born into the world on the cusp of the Long Winter?<br /> Not dealbreakers, but something to remember and an interesting sidebar at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent point, and one we considered. The concept behind the Grey is that they were born from dreams of the 'unknown', both the fear and the wonder. They had their own sort of resurgence when the War of the World radio broadcast had people in hysterics, and have been slowly trickling in since then. They have vague memories of many of earth's ancient cultures, and recall dark things chasing them from between the stars before their return. <br /> <br /> We were going to leave their history ambiguous (even to the Grey), leaving it uncertain if they are an old dream returning, or a new dream that hasounds taken form. We figured it would be best to leave it vague for the storyteller to do what they want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:57:59-07:00","id":1104029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1096650-the-book-of-modern-dreams-project?p=1103918#post1103918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an excellent point, and one we considered. The concept behind the Grey is that they were born from dreams of the 'unknown', both the fear and the wonder. They had their own sort of resurgence when the War of the World radio broadcast had people in hysterics, and have been slowly trickling in since then. They have vague memories of many of earth's ancient cultures, and recall dark things chasing them from between the stars before their return. <br /> <br /> We were going to leave their history ambiguous (even to the Grey), leaving it uncertain if they are an old dream returning, or a new dream that hasounds taken form. We figured it would be best to leave it vague for the storyteller to do what they want</div> </div> </div> </div>Creatures like the Grey are well represented in literature and esoteric belief. Luciens Moonites, the Hanon Tramp from occult lore and the many mantis-eyed entities in cave art, and others. Generally such beings were desired as tutors by occultists, but dangerous company.<br /> <br /> So greys are not new at all, though they have survived a makeover in modern terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-16-2017, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T17:55:58-07:00","id":1104557,"title":"","content":"So what is the timetable for this book? And do you want help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-17-2017, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:51:21-07:00","id":1105368,"title":"","content":"We would love help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:52:04-07:00","id":1105812,"title":"","content":"By All means we would greatly appreciate any help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}